<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simon van der Stel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1639–1712</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simon van der Stel was commander and then the first governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> from 1679 to 1699. He founded the town of Stellenbosch in 1679, encouraged settlement and wine-growing, and settled French Huguenot refugees in the colony from 1688. His estate of Groot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamis-cyprus">Constantia</a> became one of the oldest wine farms in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-van-der-stel.jpg" alt="Simon van der Stel" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pieter van Anraedt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simon_van_der_Stel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
